        "original_id": "51fa924d-4775-58ac-8e55-447ae6263bb3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Chris Brown, Jhené Aiko, James Fauntleroy, Mike Posner, Lil Wayne, Rick Ross, DJ Khaled, Big Sean\n- Groups: B2K, The Olympicks, Triple C's\n- Places: Detroit, Michigan\n- Projects: Detroit, I Am Not a Human Being, Teflon Don, Custom Cars & Cycles, Kiss The Ring\n- Topics: music careers, vocal contributions, music video appearances, hip-hop production\n\nFacts:\n- Jhené Aiko began her music career by contributing vocals and appearing in several music videos for the R&B group B2K.\n- The Olympicks originated in Detroit, Michigan.\n- The Olympicks have worked on hip-hop projects including Lil Wayne's \"I Am Not a Human Being,\" Rick Ross' \"Teflon Don,\" Triple C's \"Custom Cars & Cycles,\" and DJ Khaled's \"Kiss The Ring.\"\n- Big Sean's mixtape \"Detroit\" includes American singers Chris Brown, Jhené Aiko, James Fauntleroy, and Mike Posner.\n- The Olympicks were involved in the production of Big Sean's mixtape \"Detroit.\"",
